  "Description": {
    "Cost": 11701968,
    "Rarity": 4,
    "UIName": "Osteon",
    "Id": "chassisdef_osteon_OTN-FSN",
    "Name": "Osteon",
    "Details": "The Osteon Nuclear Suppression Variant is an experimental Society configuration designed to combine exceptional battlefield endurance with overwhelming destructive capability. Retaining the Osteon's reinforced internal structure and Ferro-Lamellor armor, the design incorporates a torso-mounted cockpit, advanced heat management systems, and Nova CEWS to improve survivability and battlefield coordination. Its primary armament consists of two Improved ATM-6 launchers equipped with experimental Society fusion nuclear warheads, allowing the OmniMech to devastate concentrated enemy formations and fortified positions. A heavy plasma cannon and two additional plasma cannons provide devastating close-range firepower, overwhelming enemy heat management systems and discouraging hostile units from closing the distance. Designed for prolonged engagements in heavily contested environments, this configuration reflects the Society's willingness to employ increasingly extreme technologies in pursuit of battlefield superiority, transforming an already formidable assault OmniMech into a walking instrument of nuclear devastation.\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Multi Trac</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.18</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limits: Omni</color>",
    "Icon": "Osteon"
  },
  "VariantName": "OTN-FSN",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitUpperLeft",
      "ArmLimitUpperRight",
      "OmniMech",
      "SocietyMech"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Juggernaut",
  "YangsThoughts": "Boss, I don't know what the hell the Society was thinking when they designed this thing. You've got an eighty-five-ton OmniMech with reinforced structure, enough Ferro-Lamellor armor to shrug off an artillery barrage, three plasma cannons to cook anything that gets close, and a pair of nuclear-tipped iATMs for everything else. I'm starting to think the armor isn't there to protect the pilot from the enemy. It's there to protect the pilot from his own damn weapons. And between you and me, Boss, if this is what the Society considers a defensive design, I'd hate to see what they use for an offensive one.",
